WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.860
[Music]

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:59.980
[Man climbs out of red work truck and begins walking away.]

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.980
[A female switchboard operator is shown turning away from the switchboard and touching her head as though it aches.]

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:11.020
[A police officer leaves headquarters.]

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:27.720
[Narrator:] In diagnosing gonorrhea, we are concerned not only with the clinical and epidemiologic evidence,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.320
but laboratory evidence as well.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:33.400
All physicians, however,  may not be equipped for laboratory diagnosis.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.760
In such circumstances it is wise to act on
a provisional diagnosis based on history

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.180
and symptoms while waiting for laboratory confirmation.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:51.459
True diagnosis rests on finding the gonococcus by study of cultures and smears,

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:54.479
or to use the word that is gaining preference, spreads.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:03:00.660
Since facilities for culture study are not available to all physicians, many must depend upon the spread alone.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.940
In any case, our concern is to secure material for laboratory study.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:19.140
The [?] discharge of acute gonorrhea makes this a simple routine matter both in the male and in the female.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.940
However a thick spread makes study difficult, so special care should be taken

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.880
to make the spread for gram staining thin and uniform.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:35.200
This is best accomplished by rolling the material in the manner shown here.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:45.089
The story is quite different in chronic gonorrhea in both sexes when the profuse discharge is not present.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:51.120
Then it is often extremely difficult to secure material for study.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.049
Yet here, careful diagnosis is most important.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:04:00.460
Chronic gonorrhea is a focus of infection and a constant source of new cases of gonorrhea.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.120
As diagnosticians, we must be familiar with those structures where the gonococcus

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:09.849
may be found and with the techniques for stripping them.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:17.160
In the male, these structures that harbor
the gonococcus are the urethra,

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.020
the prostate,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.740
Cowper's glands,

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.720
and the seminal vesicles.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.840
Stripping these structures will yield material for study.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:40.740
Of course, it is realized that procedures for stripping these structures are dangerous in the presence of acute gonorrhea

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:47.740
and that they belong only to the chronic stage of the disease and among the tests for cure.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.000
Stripping the urethra is a simple and familiar procedure.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.120
[Animated images of male genitalia and the procedure for obtaining samples of discharge for testing are shown.]

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:06.660
The prostate however, being highly susceptible
to trauma, requires gentle and correct massage.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:16.250
The safest and least painful method is to
pass the finger well up over the lateral lobe,

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.090
bringing it down in a direction parallel to the midline.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:32.550
[Animated presentation of the described procedure.]

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:37.259
After both lobes are thus emptied, the finger is passed well up beyond the median sulcus

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:43.080
of the prostate and brought several times
from there to the anterior extremity of the gland.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.730
In this form of massage, the dangers of complications are reduced.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:54.640
The patient's comfort is perhaps the best guide as to the degree of pressure to be used.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.450
Wisdom will always err on the side of gentleness.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:02.520
Cowper's glands through manipulation, may also yield material for study.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:08.159
To find the gland, the tip of the finger is
drawn down over the arch of the pubic bone,

00:06:08.169 --> 00:06:11.400
about one-half inch to the side of the midline.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.420
As it drops from the edge of the bone it will, particularly in thin patients,

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.040
fall into a triangular depression.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:23.600
The gland is easily felt by rolling the intervening tissues between the finger and the thumb.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.200
Gently rolling the tissue will express secretor lurking in the gland.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:33.080
[The described procedure is shown through animation.]

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.520
The seminal vesicles, when stripped, also provide material for study.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:42.740
However since the prostatic secretion always contains pus when the seminal vesicles are infected,

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.460
it is rarely necessary to strip them.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.800
Stripping is resorted to when vesiculitis
is suspected, but the physician should wait

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:55.670
until the acute stage of the disease has passed and the chronic stage has been reached.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:07:00.220
Only then can digital expression of the vesicles be done safely.

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:06.680
To strip the vesicles, extend the finger beyond the prostate and to the side of the midline,

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.820
and bring it downward and toward the midline as shown here.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:26.800
[The described procedure is shown through animation.]

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:32.340
With the use of these techniques, material
for spreads and cultures may be obtained

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:44.949
from the urethra, the prostate, Cowper's glands, and the seminal vesicles.

00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:50.080
Secretions obtained by stripping any of these glands are collected in sterile broth

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:53.850
for cultural studies, and stained for microscopic examination.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:09.100
[A nude man bends over an examining table, then stands up for further attention from the physician.]

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:15.160
Of course, preparation of the material for laboratory study presents no problem when the specimen is ample.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:20.320
However, stripping the urethra, the prostate, and Cowper's glands

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.090
may at times yield only a scanty discharge,

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:28.680
and in such cases the following method may be used to prepare material for study.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:33.390
After stripping the various structures, secure
the first half ounce of urine voided.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:58.140
[The male patient and the doctor are in the examining room. The doctor is handling the urine specimen.]

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.380
Then, centrifuge the urine...

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:14.040
[The doctor is hand-cranking a centrifuge.]

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:18.590
and invert the tube, so that the urine flows
out leaving the sediment in the tip of the tube.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.200
Then place a very small amount of normal salt solution in the tube,

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:47.740
[The physician carries out the described steps.]

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:52.150
and shake well so that the sediment is suspended in it.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.440
Then centrifuge again.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:17.160
Invert the tube and obtain sediment from its tip for examination.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:39.500
[The doctor continues carrying out the described procedures.]

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:44.790
This material is subjected to spread examination and where available, culture studies.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:48.660
So much for the male.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.840
Now to secure material for study in chronic
gonorrhea in the female.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:56.720
[An animated image of internal female pelvic organs is shown.]

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.320
Material may be obtained from the urethra,

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.500
from the endocervical glands,

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:16.580
and from Skene's and Bartholin's glands.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.830
To secure material for study from the urethra,

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.560
the urethral meatus is wiped with cotton to remove vulval secretions.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:42.300
[The described procedure is shown using animated images.]

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:47.550
The gloved finger is then inserted into the vagina and the urethra is stripped from above downward,

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:52.589
the external meatus being pressed
rather firmly against the pubic bone.

00:11:52.589 --> 00:11:58.289
A small cotton-wrapped applicator is inserted about half an inch into the urethra.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:02.000
The applicator should secure enough material for stain and culture.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:09.060
[An animated sequence shows the described procedure.]

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:13.860
Secretor from Skene's glands is expressed
by the procedure just described.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:16.720
No additional massage or manipulation is necessary.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:23.629
In obtaining secretor from Bartholin's glands, first wipe the area of the duct with cotton.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:27.019
[The procedure is demonstrated using animated images.]

00:12:27.019 --> 00:12:31.359
Then insert the index finger a short way into the vagina

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:35.580
and place the thumb on the outer side of the labia majora.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:40.100
The intervening tissue is then gently squeezed.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:45.260
When secretion is obtained in this way, it
is usually too scanty to be secured on an applicator.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:49.940
The flat end of a toothpick or
a platinum loop is better suited for this purpose.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:55.680
[The animated demonstration of the procedure continues.]

00:12:55.690 --> 00:13:00.160
In obtaining material from the cervix, it
is well to remember that in the chronic stage

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.700
of the disease, the gonococci are deep in
the endocervical glands,

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.940
and usually not in the plug of mucus filling the canal.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:12.440
Thus it is best to cleanse this canal with cotton held in a sponge forceps.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:23.100
[The procedure is demonstrated.]

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:26.660
Then make firm pressure on the cervix with
blades of a bivalve speculum;

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.460
And obtain the material thus expressed for
study.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.460
[Animation changes to live action as a pair of hands are shown handling the sample.]

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:51.440
If spreads of these secretions are thin and
uniform, examination will be facilitated.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:57.160
If we rely on the techniques described, we
will find that material for test and study

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.769
is always available.

00:13:58.769 --> 00:14:04.429
All of these materials from the male and the female can of course be used both for cultures and spreads.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:14.300
[A cylindrical container with the sample is shown.]

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:18.620
Mastery of these techniques will help provide laboratory evidence for diagnosis,

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:23.360
and what is equally important: laboratory confirmation of cure.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:27.940
[A female laboratory worker is shown testing samples,]

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:32.140
But, as the laboratory checks the clinical
symptoms and general treatment,

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.920
so in the case of chronic gonorrhea in the female,

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:40.699
the clinical symptoms and case history must be used as a check on the laboratory.

00:14:40.699 --> 00:14:45.499
This is necessary because in chronic gonorrhea in women, the gonococcus will sometimes

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:50.000
escape detection by both the gram stain and the culture.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.650
Consequently, when the history is suspicious
and symptoms persist,

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:58.620
the laboratory must be challenged, perhaps repudiated.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.180
In the case of the female with chronic gonorrhea,

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:06.940
we must be guided by epidemiologic and clinical evidence as well as by laboratory evidence.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:14.600
If symptoms and history point to the gonococcus, treatment is definitely in order.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:21.760
[A physician appears to be reviewing lab reports with a female patient, asking questions to which she replies.]

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:28.760
To withhold treatment is to risk new infections and grave complications for the patient.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:42.340
In any case, the procedure of treating on
suspicion cannot be challenged.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:45.920
We all know patients who come for examination and never return.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:50.460
We know that often we have a positive diagnosis from the laboratory, but no patient.

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:58.560
[The doctor is now seated in his office with a male patient.]

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:03.560
To treat on suspicion, to warn at once that
an infectious disease may be present

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:08.200
and to urge the patient to act accordingly, is to move towards gonorrhea control.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:19.960
[The male patient puts on his hat and leaves. A nurse comes in to speak to the doctor.]

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:23.340
Certainly, where infectious diseases are concerned,

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:28.140
every physician feels that his responsibility extends beyond his patient.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:31.200
It extends to the people the patient may infect.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:37.220
[The male patient who has just left the office walks away with a woman who was standing outside the building.]

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:46.120
Since diagnosis is an integral part of the
patient's first visit, and this first encounter

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:50.880
with the physician has a profound influence on the patient's later behavior,

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:55.040
it may be in order to discuss further at this point, the patient and his doctor.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:17:01.339
Effective venereal disease control and good
case-holding rests on the doctor-patient relationship

00:17:01.339 --> 00:17:05.510
and require that the patient be considered
as a total medical problem.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:08.630
The patient must be given an understanding of the nature of his problem,

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:13.540
and he must be given an objective, which will impel him to continue treatment.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:18.460
The patient may have syphilis. There may be other complications.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:23.880
Certainly, in a patient with gonorrheal infection, syphilis must be considered.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:28.770
Ideally, the history of gonorrhea case follows these general lines.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:36.200
The patient usually  comes to the doctor's office three to six days after exposure, when the symptoms appear.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:42.980
Following the examination, the doctor takes material for a spread.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:49.380
He also takes a blood test for syphilis as part of the physical examination.

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:54.880
It is too early to check for a syphilitic infection which may have been contracted when gonorrhea was contracted.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:59.000
But the doctor explains that the danger of such an infection exists.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:04.270
If possible, the doctor then gets the name of the contact and speaks of bringing her under treatment,

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.820
He also explains the nature of the disease to the patient,

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:10.660
in language that the patient can understand.

00:18:18.669 --> 00:18:25.669
The patient returns in three days for a second
examination and to learn the laboratory findings.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:29.500
Let us assume that the findings of the test
for syphilis are negative.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.900
The smear, however, is positive.

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:38.120
Since treatment began with the first visit,
the doctor now simply checks the progress of the disease.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:47.900
Seven days later, the symptoms of most patients will have vanished.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:55.100
But now enough time may have elapsed for penile lesions to appear, if the patient also contracted syphilis.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:19:00.500
The doctor looks for lesions and if he finds
them, does a darkfield test at once.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:04.440
Let us assume that no lesions are found at this time.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.600
The patient returns again in seven days for two reasons:

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:11.400
so that the doctor can check the gonorrhea cure,

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.340
and look for penile lesions again.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.900
We assume that again, no lesions are found.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:25.560
The patient returns and is reexamined for infectious lesions at weekly intervals for three weeks.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.720
Thereafter, every two weeks, for another six weeks.

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:34.240
A second blood test is part of the final examination.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.620
We have thus completed a three-month period of observation.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:42.820
The course of action described here has given the patient the fullest possible protection.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:48.680
His gonorrhea cure has been determined; the physician has also determined whether or not there was a syphilitic infection.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:54.670
The results are good case-holding and effective venereal disease control.

00:19:54.679 --> 00:20:00.039
These are objectives that must be attained.
We know only too well that they will never come

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:06.100
to us from the laboratory, but only from
an appreciation of human relationships.

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:16.880
When we speak of chemotherapy, we speak of the weapon with which a change in history has been wrought.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:20.960
We speak of a swift, sure,
and inexpensive cure for gonorrhea.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:26.140
Chemotherapy in gonorrhea has made difficult and painful local treatment unnecessary,

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:30.100
except in the small number of patients who do not respond to such medication.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:35.770
It is a great boon to the private physician,
to clinics carrying heavy caseloads,

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:42.020
often with extremely limited personnel, and of course it is a great boon to the patient.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:47.220
In discussing this new treatment, it may be
well to recall an era of the past,

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:50.160
in order to dispose of it permanently for the future.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:54.660
Sulfonilamide was the first sulfa drug used
in the treatment of gonorrhea.

00:20:54.680 --> 00:21:00.180
Although toxic reactions were frequent and sometimes grave, it continued in use for a time

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:04.420
because a better substitute was not yet found.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:12.060
Because to tens of thousands infected with
gonorrhea, it offered the promise of a swift cure,

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:16.660
a swift return to the jobs from which
the disease had taken them.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:21.640
This early sulfonamide compound held out a hope to gonorrhea sufferers.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:32.140
[A cross-section of people, wearing suits, work clothes, and uniforms, assembles in a line.]

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:39.180
But sulfanilamide produced toxic reactions
in many patients and created numerous asymptomatic carriers.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:44.080
Laboratories focused their attention on finding a safer and more effective chemotherapeutic agent.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:50.280
New sulfa drugs were produced rapidly. Drugs superior to sulfanilamide.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.220
As these more effective drugs appeared,

00:21:53.340 --> 00:22:00.400
leading clinicians and the United States Public Health Service abandoned sulfanilamide.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:06.200
But sulfanilamide had been widely publicized, and so it gave way but slowly

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:10.240
to the more effective, safer drugs.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:16.400
Doctors continued to prescribe it. Patients
continued to ask for it.

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:22.060
But there is no place for sulfanilamide in the treatment of gonorrhea.

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:28.100
Today, the drug of choice is sulfathiazole.

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:34.540
But research and experience indicate that
it may be entirely supplanted by penicillin.

00:22:36.409 --> 00:22:39.760
The toxicity of penicillin is negligible.

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:47.080
The toxicity of sulfathiazole is low and the
reactions are mild.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:52.419
Rarely does the patient find it impossible to consume enough of the drug to bring about a cure.

00:22:52.419 --> 00:22:58.789
Even when low blood concentrations are maintained, a relatively high cure rate is achieved.

00:22:58.789 --> 00:23:03.609
Of course, there are a few people who cannot tolerate any of the sulfa drugs in any concentration,

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:06.330
and so all patients must be watched.

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:11.300
This is no drug to be sold over a counter, without a prescription.

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:15.900
Twenty grams is the recommended dosage for a single course of treatment;

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:19.360
four grams a day for five days.

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:28.620
However, if this first course of sulfathiazole fails to bring about a cure,

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:37.260
medication should be discontinued for seven to ten days, and then a second course of treatment given.

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:45.620
A number of patients will not be cured. Penicillin should be considered.

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:50.400
Penicillin therapy of gonorrhea may mock or delay symptoms of syphilis.

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:54.700
Patient observation should be continued over three months.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:58.670
As special precaution against transmitting
a possible chronic infection,

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:04.470
the physician should insist that a condom be used at every sexual contact for three months

00:24:04.470 --> 00:24:06.190
after disappearance of symptoms.

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:14.290
With the aid of these drugs, we can in a short
time make gonorrhea a comparatively rare disease.

00:24:14.290 --> 00:24:29.130
[People are shown walking, arriving at their jobs, and conducting their usual daily business.]

00:24:32.460 --> 00:24:36.120
Prophylaxis is the other great ally of gonorrhea control.

00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:42.480
Civilian and military health authorities now recognize its value and urge its widespread use.

00:24:42.860 --> 00:24:47.100
To make descriptions of approved techniques available to physicians,

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:52.040
these publications have been prepared and are furnished on request.

00:24:52.040 --> 00:24:57.480
The greatest safety and preventive measures, other than continence, belongs to the condom.

00:24:57.720 --> 00:25:02.060
But improper use of the condom destroys its value.

00:25:06.860 --> 00:25:12.580
Instruction of the patient is part of the
physician's role in implementing prophylaxis.

00:25:12.590 --> 00:25:17.419
Common habits such as using a condom only
at the end of intercourse should be condemned.

00:25:17.419 --> 00:25:22.929
The patient should also be warned to put on the condom before his hand comes into contact

00:25:22.929 --> 00:25:28.489
with the woman's genitalia, lest he carry
the infection to his own organs before intercourse is begun.

00:25:28.970 --> 00:25:32.190
These and other points need to be impressed on the patient.

00:25:32.600 --> 00:25:39.620
The pamphlet shown is intended for lay education and can also be secured from the United States Public Health Service.

00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:47.720
The prophylactic packet is sometimes effective but here again, the patient needs instruction as to its proper use.

00:25:47.820 --> 00:25:52.980
Chemical prophylaxis is most effective when administered under medical supervision.

00:25:53.360 --> 00:25:58.300
When administered soon after exposure, it is at least 90 percent effective.

00:25:58.440 --> 00:26:04.640
Prophylactic measures are not as easily applied in women. Nor are they considered to be as efficacious.

00:26:04.650 --> 00:26:12.310
There is no doubt that widespread use of prophylaxis will aid materially in controlling gonorrhea.

00:26:14.800 --> 00:26:21.720
Education of the public so that people will
not go to the quack, but to the licensed physician...

00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:33.400
early diagnosis by the physician; correct
use of prophylaxis; sulfathiazole; penicillin...

00:26:33.560 --> 00:26:41.160
these things are weapons in the hands of the medical profession.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:49.720
And most important in gonorrhea therapy, let
us remember this: a laboratory is not infallible.

00:26:51.140 --> 00:26:57.340
Clinical and epidemiologic findings are ample
grounds for treatment.

00:26:57.340 --> 00:27:02.360
If we use them as a basis for treatment, we
will eradicate many infections

00:27:02.360 --> 00:27:05.940
that in the past filtered through the diagnostic net.

00:27:05.950 --> 00:27:11.809
Certainly sulfathiazole and penicillin are
a promise and a challenge to the medical profession,

00:27:11.809 --> 00:27:17.350
an opportunity to wipe out one of our oldest
diseases, and an opportunity to save millions

00:27:17.350 --> 00:27:21.220
of man-days lost to industry and the armed
forces...

00:27:21.220 --> 00:27:25.009
to prevent a great loss to the nation's health and strength.

00:27:25.380 --> 00:27:40.720
[Music]

